<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat falls in step with U.S. market.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat falls in step with U.S. market.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sydney wheat futures traded lower in modest volumes on Friday.</p>
<p>November showed the biggest loss, dropping A$4.50 to settle at A$154.00 a tonne.</p>
<p>The other two traded contracts, January and May 1997, each shed A$2.50 to close A$154.00 and A$157.50 a tonne, respectively.</p>
<p>Wheat traders said the local market came under the influence of overnight U.S. trading, which saw CBOT wheat prices at contract lows. &quot;People saw what was going on in Chicago and decided it was time to get short,&quot; one said.</p>
